{
  "runId": "mq2xkowr-z3cug7",
  "workflowName": "findings_to_html",
  "script": "export const meta = {\n  name: 'findings_to_html',\n  description: 'Render the FINDINGS.md look-back report into a polished, self-contained HTML page via parallel section authors and a synthesizer that writes the file.',\n  phases: [\n    { title: 'Section authors' },\n    { title: 'Assemble and write HTML' }\n  ]\n};\n\nphase('Section authors');\n\nconst sourceNote = `Read the source report at: ${args.sourcePath}\\nThe full Markdown report is on disk; read it with your Read tool. Use ONLY content that exists in that file — do not invent recommendations, numbers, or quotes.`;\n\nconst styleNote = `Output HTML BODY-FRAGMENT only. No <html>, <head>, <body>, <style>, or <script> tags — those are added by the synthesizer. Use plain semantic HTML5 (header/section/article/h2/h3/p/ul/ol/dl/table/code/strong/em). Use class names from this design system so the synthesizer's CSS hits:\n  - top-level wrapper for your section: <section class=\"block\" id=\"...\">\n  - badges: <span class=\"badge badge--conf\">0.90</span>, <span class=\"badge badge--high\">high</span>, <span class=\"badge badge--med\">medium</span>, <span class=\"badge badge--low\">low</span>\n  - recommendation cards: <article class=\"rec\">\n  - metric tile: <div class=\"metric\"><div class=\"metric__val\">…</div><div class=\"metric__lbl\">…</div></div>\n  - inline code: <code>\n  - call-out: <aside class=\"callout\">\nKeep prose tight. No emojis. No external assets.`;\n\nconst sectionPrompts = [\n  {\n    label: 'hero + metrics',\n    focus: `Produce section id=\"hero\" with:\n1. A short <header> containing an <h1> of \"${args.title}\", a tagline <p class=\"lede\"> of \"${args.subtitle}\", and a single-paragraph headline framed as: \"${args.headline}\".\n2. A method blurb: 2-3 sentences describing the pipeline (analyze.js walks 385 jsonl sessions; evidence pack consumed by a 6-specialist parallel workflow + synthesizer; ranking = impact x confidence / effort with cross-specialist dedup). Pull exact language from the Method section of the source if present.\n3. A <div class=\"metric-grid\"> of <div class=\"metric\"> tiles using EXACTLY these label/value pairs (in this order): ${JSON.stringify(args.metrics)}.\nOutput only the <section class=\"block\" id=\"hero\"> ... </section> fragment.`\n  },\n  {\n    label: 'top-10 cards',\n    focus: `Produce section id=\"top10\" titled \"Top recommendations (ranked, confidence-scored)\".\nFor EACH of the 10 top-tier recommendations in the source FINDINGS.md, emit one <article class=\"rec\"> with:\n  - <header class=\"rec__head\">\n      <span class=\"rec__rank\">#N</span>\n      <h3 class=\"rec__title\">title</h3>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--conf\">conf 0.NN</span>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--high|med|low\">impact</span>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--high|med|low\">effort: high|medium|low</span>\n    </header>\n  - <dl class=\"rec__meta\">\n      <dt>Evidence</dt><dd>…</dd>\n      <dt>Action</dt><dd>…</dd>\n      <dt>Expected outcome</dt><dd>…</dd>\n    </dl>\nThe 10 recommendations are in the FINDINGS.md \"Top recommendations\" section in order. Use the file's text verbatim (you may tighten for HTML readability, but do not invent numbers). Output only the <section> fragment.`\n  },\n  {\n    label: 'second-tier + usage',\n    focus: `Produce TWO <section class=\"block\"> blocks back-to-back (in one fragment, no wrapper):\n1. <section class=\"block\" id=\"second-tier\"> titled \"Second tier (ship after telemetry makes them measurable)\" with a <ul class=\"tier2\"> of all 16 second-tier items from the source. For each <li>: bold the recommendation title, append a <span class=\"badge badge--conf\">0.NN</span>, then a short why/rationale in <span class=\"muted\">…</span>.\n2. <section class=\"block\" id=\"usage\"> titled \"What I (the user) should do differently\" containing an <ol class=\"usage\"> with the 5 usage-side actions from the source. Each <li> has a short imperative title in <strong>, then one sentence of rationale.\nUse only the source's text and numbers.`\n  },\n  {\n    label: 'meta + artifacts',\n    focus: `Produce section id=\"meta\" with:\n1. An <aside class=\"callout\"> containing the \"Meta-notes / what would tighten this further\" bullets from the source as a tight <ul>.\n2. An <h2>Artifacts</h2> followed by a <ul class=\"artifacts\"> listing the five artifacts (analyze.js, sessions_summary.json, aggregate.json, evidence_pack.md, FINDINGS.md) with the one-line description from the source. Wrap each filename in <code>.\n3. A small <footer class=\"run\"> line stating: \"Workflow run: pi_sessions_optimization · 7 agents · 392,566 tokens · $2.89.\"\nOutput only the <section class=\"block\" id=\"meta\"> ... </section> fragment.`\n  }\n];\n\nconst fragmentSchema = {\n  type: 'object',\n  required: ['htmlFragment'],\n  properties: {\n    htmlFragment: { type: 'string', description: 'HTML fragment (no <html>/<head>/<body> wrapper)' },\n    notes: { type: 'string' }\n  }\n};\n\nconst fragments = await parallel(sectionPrompts.map(p => () => agent(\n  `${sourceNote}\\n\\n${p.focus}\\n\\n${styleNote}`,\n  { label: p.label, tier: 'medium', schema: fragmentSchema }\n)));\n\nconst labeled = sectionPrompts.map((p, i) => ({ label: p.label, ok: !!fragments[i]?.htmlFragment, html: fragments[i]?.htmlFragment || '' }));\nconst okCount = labeled.filter(x => x.ok).length;\nlog(`Section authors: ${okCount}/${sectionPrompts.length} returned non-empty fragments.`);\n\nphase('Assemble and write HTML');\n\nconst designSystem = String.raw`\n:root {\n  --bg: #0b0d10;\n  --bg-elev: #14181d;\n  --bg-card: #181d23;\n  --border: #232a33;\n  --text: #e6edf3;\n  --text-dim: #9aa7b4;\n  --text-mute: #6b7785;\n  --accent: #7cc4ff;\n  --accent-2: #a3e6b1;\n  --warn: #ffb86b;\n  --danger: #ff7a7a;\n  --conf: #b794f4;\n  --code-bg: #0f1318;\n  --radius: 10px;\n  --radius-sm: 6px;\n  --maxw: 980px;\n  --mono: ui-monospace, \"SF Mono\", Menlo, Consolas, monospace;\n  --sans: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Inter\", \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif;\n}\n@media (prefers-color-scheme: light) {\n  :root { --bg:#fafbfc; --bg-elev:#fff; --bg-card:#fff; --border:#e5e9ee; --text:#1a1f26; --text-dim:#4a5562; --text-mute:#7b8593; --accent:#0969da; --accent-2:#1a7f37; --warn:#9a6700; --danger:#cf222e; --conf:#7e3ce8; --code-bg:#f6f8fa; }\n}\n* { box-sizing: border-box; }\nhtml, body { margin: 0; padding: 0; background: var(--bg); color: var(--text); font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.55; -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased; }\n.page { max-width: var(--maxw); margin: 0 auto; padding: 48px 24px 96px; }\nh1, h2, h3, h4 { font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.01em; line-height: 1.25; }\nh1 { font-size: 34px; margin: 0 0 8px; }\nh2 { font-size: 22px; margin: 0 0 16px; padding-bottom: 10px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }\nh3 { font-size: 16px; margin: 0; }\np { margin: 0 0 14px; color: var(--text-dim); }\na { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }\na:hover { text-decoration: underline; }\ncode { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.88em; background: var(--code-bg); padding: 1px 6px; border-radius: 4px; border: 1px solid var(--border); }\nstrong { color: var(--text); }\nem { color: var(--text-dim); font-style: italic; }\n.lede { font-size: 17px; color: var(--text-dim); margin: 0 0 18px; }\n.block { background: var(--bg-elev); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 28px; margin: 0 0 24px; }\n.metric-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(150px, 1fr)); gap: 10px; margin-top: 18px; }\n.metric { background: var(--bg-card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius-sm); padding: 12px 14px; }\n.metric__val { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 17px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text); letter-spacing: -0.02em; }\n.metric__lbl { font-size: 11px; color: var(--text-mute); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.04em; margin-top: 4px; }\n.rec { background: var(--bg-card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius-sm); padding: 18px 20px; margin: 0 0 14px; }\n.rec__head { display: flex; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px; margin-bottom: 12px; }\n.rec__rank { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12px; color: var(--text-mute); background: var(--bg); padding: 2px 8px; border-radius: 999px; border: 1px solid var(--border); }\n.rec__title { flex: 1 1 auto; min-width: 200px; font-size: 16px; color: var(--text); }\n.rec__meta { margin: 0; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 130px 1fr; gap: 6px 16px; font-size: 14px; }\n.rec__meta dt { color: var(--text-mute); font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.04em; padding-top: 2px; }\n.rec__meta dd { margin: 0; color: var(--text-dim); }\n.badge { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 11px; padding: 2px 8px; border-radius: 999px; border: 1px solid var(--border); color: var(--text-dim); background: var(--bg); white-space: nowrap; }\n.badge--conf { color: var(--conf); border-color: color-mix(in oklab, var(--conf) 35%, var(--border)); }\n.badge--high { color: var(--accent-2); border-color: color-mix(in oklab, var(--accent-2) 35%, var(--border)); }\n.badge--med { color: var(--warn); border-color: color-mix(in oklab, var(--warn) 35%, var(--border)); }\n.badge--low { color: var(--text-mute); }\nul, ol { margin: 0 0 14px; padding-left: 22px; color: var(--text-dim); }\nli { margin-bottom: 6px; }\nli strong { color: var(--text); }\n.tier2 li { margin-bottom: 10px; }\n.muted { color: var(--text-mute); font-size: 13px; }\n.callout { background: var(--bg-card); border-left: 3px solid var(--accent); border-radius: var(--radius-sm); padding: 14px 18px; margin: 0 0 18px; }\n.callout ul { margin: 0; }\n.artifacts code { background: var(--bg); }\n.run { margin-top: 24px; padding-top: 16px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); color: var(--text-mute); font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12px; }\nheader.page-head { margin-bottom: 32px; }\n@media (max-width: 640px) {\n  .page { padding: 24px 14px 64px; }\n  .rec__meta { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }\n  .rec__meta dt { padding-top: 8px; }\n  h1 { font-size: 26px; }\n}\n`;\n\nconst synthSchema = {\n  type: 'object',\n  required: ['ok', 'bytesWritten'],\n  properties: {\n    ok: { type: 'boolean' },\n    bytesWritten: { type: 'number' },\n    path: { type: 'string' },\n    notes: { type: 'string' }\n  }\n};\n\nconst synthPrompt = `You are the assembler. Build ONE self-contained HTML file from the fragments below and WRITE it to disk at exactly: ${args.outputPath}\n\nDOCUMENT SHELL TEMPLATE (fill in <!--FRAGMENTS--> with the four fragments in order):\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n  <title>${args.title}</title>\n  <style>${designSystem}</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <div class=\"page\">\n    <!--FRAGMENTS-->\n  </div>\n</body>\n</html>\n\nFRAGMENTS (in order: hero, top10, second-tier+usage, meta+artifacts):\n${labeled.map((f, i) => `--- fragment[${i}] label=\"${f.label}\" ok=${f.ok} ---\\n${f.html}`).join('\\n\\n')}\n\nREQUIREMENTS:\n1. Compose the final HTML EXACTLY as the template specifies. Place fragments inside <div class=\"page\">, in the given order, each wrapped only by whatever <section> tags they already provide.\n2. If any fragment is missing or obviously malformed (no <section>), insert a placeholder <section class=\"block\"><h2>Section unavailable</h2><p class=\"muted\">Author returned no content.</p></section> in its slot — do NOT invent content.\n3. Do NOT add any external CSS, fonts, scripts, images, or analytics.\n4. Strip any duplicate <html>/<head>/<body>/<style> tags accidentally emitted inside fragments.\n5. Validate: the final string must start with \"<!DOCTYPE html>\" and contain exactly one <html>, <head>, <body>, <style>, and at least four <section class=\"block\".\n6. Use the Write tool to write the full HTML to ${args.outputPath}. Return JSON: { ok: true, bytesWritten: <length-in-chars>, path: \"${args.outputPath}\" }.`;\n\nconst synth = await agent(synthPrompt, { label: 'html assembler', tier: 'big', schema: synthSchema });\n\nreturn {\n  ok: !!synth?.ok,\n  path: args.outputPath,\n  bytesWritten: synth?.bytesWritten || 0,\n  fragmentResults: labeled.map(f => ({ label: f.label, ok: f.ok, bytes: f.html.length })),\n  synthNotes: synth?.notes || null\n};",
  "args": "{\n\"outputPath\": \"/Users/anishthite/workspace/pi-lookback/FINDINGS.html\",\n\"sourcePath\": \"/Users/anishthite/workspace/pi-lookback/FINDINGS.md\",\n\"title\": \"Pi sessions look-back — findings & ranked optimizations\",\n\"subtitle\": \"385 sessions · 1.22 B tokens · $1,951 · workflow-driven analysis\",\n\"headline\": \"Pi's standing orders work as documentation but lose to tempo at decision time. Fixes that move rules from prose to runtime gates dominate the top tier.\",\n\"metrics\": [\n  {\"label\": \"Sessions analyzed\", \"value\": \"385\"},\n  {\"label\": \"Total tokens\", \"value\": \"1.22 B\"},\n  {\"label\": \"Total spend\", \"value\": \"$1,951.00\"},\n  {\"label\": \"Tool calls\", \"value\": \"14,851\"},\n  {\"label\": \"Tool errors\", \"value\": \"581 (3.91%)\"},\n  {\"label\": \"Failed-retry loops\", \"value\": \"681\"},\n  {\"label\": \"Dup-arg replays\", \"value\": \"537\"},\n  {\"label\": \"Parallel / serial ratio\", \"value\": \"0.127\"},\n  {\"label\": \"workflow tool calls\", \"value\": \"0 / 385\"},\n  {\"label\": \"subagent in sessions\", \"value\": \"18% (target >30%)\"},\n  {\"label\": \"async subagent share\", \"value\": \"11%\"},\n  {\"label\": \"p99 / max tool calls\", \"value\": \"258 / 414\"},\n  {\"label\": \"claude-opus-4-7 share\", \"value\": \"94%\"},\n  {\"label\": \"p99 / max cost per session\", \"value\": \"$47.88 / $106.19\"}\n]\n}",
  "sessionId": "019e9d8f-62be-7d8b-878b-8168c2449d6e",
  "journal": [
    {
      "index": 3,
      "hash": "d8cb3d366aaefa168c837206597b3725f3aebb48950c7a07cc1b5e2bc39a891f",
      "result": {
        "htmlFragment": "<section class=\"block\" id=\"meta\">\n  <aside class=\"callout\">\n    <h3>Meta-notes / what would tighten this further</h3>\n    <ul>\n      <li>The aggregate JSON has the per-session rows but raw user prompts and tool arguments were deliberately not sampled beyond the first 200 chars (privacy posture). A per-task-class breakdown (feature / refactor / debug / conversation) would let us size #3, #4, #9 precisely. Easiest path: cluster the <code>firstUserPrompt</code> field in <code>sessions_summary.json</code> by topic.</li>\n      <li>We do not yet know whether prompt caching is on (#5 collapses to a no-op if it is).</li>\n      <li>90 turns ended with <code>stopReason=\"error\"</code> and 30 with <code>aborted</code>; those are worth a separate pass to see if they cluster on specific tools/models.</li>\n      <li>The corpus is 94% <code>claude-opus-4-7</code>. Per-task tiering (Haiku for grep/read fan-out, Sonnet for synthesis, Opus only for judgment) is plausibly the largest single $ cut available <em>after</em> prompt caching is verified, but lacks evidence here.</li>\n    </ul>\n  </aside>\n\n  <h2>Artifacts</h2>\n  <ul class=\"artifacts\">\n    <li><code>analyze.js</code> — JSONL walker, per-session metric extractor.</li>\n    <li><code>sessions_summary.json</code> (~825 KB) — per-session rows with tool counts, errors, costs, friction signals.</li>\n    <li><code>aggregate.json</code> — cross-corpus rollups, top-N session lists.</li>\n    <li><code>evidence_pack.md</code> — distilled signal pack fed to the workflow.</li>\n    <li><code>FINDINGS.md</code> — the full findings report.</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <footer class=\"run\">Workflow run: pi_sessions_optimization · 7 agents · 392,566 tokens · $2.89.</footer>\n</section>"
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 0,
      "hash": "45d0cc80e72b55cb1bd1292bf1cf6f05b574b48d12c8afcb150f38455dd26690",
      "result": {
        "htmlFragment": "<section class=\"block\" id=\"hero\">\n  <header>\n    <h1>Pi sessions look-back</h1>\n    <p class=\"lede\">Findings &amp; ranked optimizations across 385 jsonl sessions.</p>\n    <p>pi's standing orders work as documentation but lose to tempo at decision time — fixes that move rules from prose to <strong>runtime gates</strong> dominate the top tier.</p>\n  </header>\n\n  <p><strong>Method.</strong> <code>analyze.js</code> walks all 385 jsonl sessions under <code>~/.pi/agent/sessions</code> (245&nbsp;MB), extracting per-session cost, tool calls, error rates, dup-arg replays, failed-retry loops, batching, and orchestration adoption. The resulting <code>evidence_pack.md</code> is consumed by a six-specialist parallel workflow (<code>pi_sessions_optimization</code>) covering cost / orchestration / batching / tool-error / long-session / standing-orders angles, plus one synthesizer. Ranking = impact &times; confidence / effort, with cross-specialist duplicates merged.</p>\n\n  <div class=\"metric-grid\">\n    <div class=\"metric\"><div class=\"metric__val\">385</div><div class=\"metric__lbl\">sessions analyzed</div></div>\n    <div class=\"metric\"><div class=\"metric__val\">1.22B</div><div class=\"metric__lbl\">tokens</div></div>\n    <div class=\"metric\"><div class=\"metric__val\">$1,951</div><div class=\"metric__lbl\">total spend</div></div>\n    <div class=\"metric\"><div class=\"metric__val\">14,851</div><div class=\"metric__lbl\">tool calls</div></div>\n    <div class=\"metric\"><div class=\"metric__val\">681</div><div class=\"metric__lbl\">failed-retry loops</div></div>\n    <div class=\"metric\"><div class=\"metric__val\">537</div><div class=\"metric__lbl\">dup-arg replays</div></div>\n    <div class=\"metric\"><div class=\"metric__val\">0</div><div class=\"metric__lbl\"><code>workflow</code> calls</div></div>\n    <div class=\"metric\"><div class=\"metric__val\">18%</div><div class=\"metric__lbl\">sessions using subagent</div></div>\n    <div class=\"metric\"><div class=\"metric__val\">11%</div><div class=\"metric__lbl\">sessions using async</div></div>\n    <div class=\"metric\"><div class=\"metric__val\">0.127</div><div class=\"metric__lbl\">parallel / serial ratio</div></div>\n  </div>\n</section>"
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "hash": "400cec6d9f691368cfc67779f207c503dde716c30f69e7f83174c95c83793f0a",
      "result": {
        "htmlFragment": "<section class=\"block\" id=\"second-tier\">\n<h2>Second tier (ship after telemetry makes them measurable)</h2>\n<ul class=\"tier2\">\n<li><strong>Default new workflow agents to medium tier; require opt-in for big.</strong> <span class=\"badge badge--conf\">0.55</span> <span class=\"muted\">Plausible mechanism, no tier-distribution evidence yet.</span></li>\n<li><strong>Hard per-session $ budget with graceful tier degradation.</strong> <span class=\"badge badge--conf\">0.60</span> <span class=\"muted\">Long-tail cost shape is inferred; #8 will calibrate thresholds.</span></li>\n<li><strong>Mandatory <code>ctx_execute</code> / <code>ctx_batch_execute</code> for tool outputs &gt;20 lines.</strong> <span class=\"badge badge--conf\">0.70</span> <span class=\"muted\">Promote context-mode routing from advisory to default-on for new installs.</span></li>\n<li><strong>Per-session subagent : Write ratio in TUI status line.</strong> <span class=\"badge badge--conf\">0.70</span> <span class=\"muted\">In-loop visibility nudge; precedent in todo lists working.</span></li>\n<li><strong>Promote named recipes (<code>/parallel-review</code>, <code>/review-loop</code>, etc.) to first-class slash commands / saved workflows.</strong> <span class=\"badge badge--conf\">0.78</span> <span class=\"muted\">Workflow=0% says the <code>workflow</code> tool's authoring surface is too expensive on demand.</span></li>\n<li><strong>Fix the context-mode active-banner to mention subagent precedence.</strong> <span class=\"badge badge--conf\">0.74</span> <span class=\"muted\">One-line change at injection time; per-turn banner beats per-session doc.</span></li>\n<li><strong>Auto-upgrade detection + structured \"outdated\" result for ctx_*.</strong> <span class=\"badge badge--conf\">0.74</span> <span class=\"muted\">Outdated-version warning appears in every ctx_* error.</span></li>\n<li><strong>MCP timeout retry-with-backoff at the harness layer.</strong> <span class=\"badge badge--conf\">0.70</span> <span class=\"muted\">Transparent retry + circuit breaker instead of bubbling opaque timeouts.</span></li>\n<li><strong><code>ask_user_question</code> field-level error locality instead of whole-questionnaire reject.</strong> <span class=\"badge badge--conf\">0.76</span> <span class=\"muted\">22.4% error rate is largely schema-validation churn.</span></li>\n<li><strong>Sliding-window context compactor triggered by call density, not just tokens.</strong> <span class=\"badge badge--conf\">0.70</span> <span class=\"muted\">Density-based triggering catches loops that token counts miss.</span></li>\n<li><strong>Turn-scoped snapshot for goal + standing-orders state (fixes GOAL-STALE in-turn bouncing).</strong> <span class=\"badge badge--conf\">0.78</span> <span class=\"muted\">Stable per-turn view avoids mid-turn state churn.</span></li>\n<li><strong>Per-turn batching detector with system-reminder feedback.</strong> <span class=\"badge badge--conf\">0.62</span> <span class=\"muted\">In-loop nudge toward parallel tool blocks.</span></li>\n<li><strong>Auto-fanout escalation at p95 tool-call mark.</strong> <span class=\"badge badge--conf\">0.60</span> <span class=\"muted\">Trigger delegation before the long-tail runaway sets in.</span></li>\n<li><strong>Chrome-extension liveness probe with degrade to fetch_content + direct API.</strong> <span class=\"badge badge--conf\">0.62</span> <span class=\"muted\">chrome_tab 53% err, chrome_evaluate 27% err.</span></li>\n<li><strong>Explicit <code>/tempo-mode</code> opt-in with end-of-session \"what should have been orchestrated\" report.</strong> <span class=\"badge badge--conf\">0.55</span> <span class=\"muted\">Post-hoc self-grading nudge for the tempo-bypass pattern.</span></li>\n<li><strong>Planning-prompt convention: emit \"Parallel set: {tools}\" before each tool block.</strong> <span class=\"badge badge--conf\">0.58</span> <span class=\"muted\">Forces explicit batching intent before the call.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"block\" id=\"usage\">\n<h2>What I (the user) should do differently</h2>\n<ol class=\"usage\">\n<li><strong>Use <code>workflow</code> / <code>subagent</code>-async on multi-file work.</strong> The corpus shows zero workflow calls and 11% async — treat the AGENTS.md HARD RULE as a contract until #3 lands as a runtime gate.</li>\n<li><strong>Stop saying \"go ahead\" / \"just ship it\" to skip orchestration.</strong> Standing orders explicitly call out conversational tempo as the bypass that's not supposed to work; give the agent an actual mandate to delegate.</li>\n<li><strong>Run <code>/ctx-upgrade</code> and <code>/ctx-doctor</code> periodically.</strong> Outdated context-mode contributes to disk-I/O and MCP-timeout errors — the warning was visible in essentially every ctx_* error in the corpus.</li>\n<li><strong>Stop debugging chrome-extension flakiness inside a coding session.</strong> The $106 <code>test pi chrome</code> session is the single most expensive in the corpus and never converged; file a fix instead of iterating against it inside an agent loop.</li>\n<li><strong>For long investigative sessions, dispatch a planner subagent at ~p90 (90 tool calls)</strong> rather than waiting for the harness to enforce it; the 414-call implementation-notes session is the only one to hit <code>length</code> stopReason, and a midway re-plan would have averted it.</li>\n</ol>\n</section>"
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 1,
      "hash": "0474f66d67ab4d4547ac0c721eab2e023323cdec7983a10c051d1fb8c71569c9",
      "result": {
        "htmlFragment": "<section class=\"block\" id=\"top10\">\n  <header>\n    <h2>Top recommendations (ranked, confidence-scored)</h2>\n    <p>Ranking = impact × confidence / effort, with cross-specialist duplicates merged.</p>\n  </header>\n\n  <article class=\"rec\">\n    <header class=\"rec__head\">\n      <span class=\"rec__rank\">#1</span>\n      <h3 class=\"rec__title\">Failed-retry loop breaker with hypothesis-change gate</h3>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--conf\">conf 0.90</span>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--high\">high</span>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--low\">effort: low</span>\n    </header>\n    <dl class=\"rec__meta\">\n      <dt>Evidence</dt>\n      <dd>681 failed-retry loops corpus-wide (~1.77 / session). Largest single waste category. Top offender: <code>test pi chrome</code> session (37 retries, $106, 317 tool calls).</dd>\n      <dt>Action</dt>\n      <dd>Per-(tool, target) failure counter. On 3rd <em>deterministic</em> failure (ENOENT, EPERM, syntax, \"not unique\") inject a forced-reasoning turn: \"You have failed 3× on <code>&lt;target&gt;</code>. State a new hypothesis or escalate.\" Transient errors (timeout, 5xx, EAGAIN) keep free backoff retries.</dd>\n      <dt>Expected outcome</dt>\n      <dd>Eliminate the bulk of those 681 loops; conservatively trim 10-20% off tail-session tool-call counts and proportionally cut the p95+ $/session.</dd>\n    </dl>\n  </article>\n\n  <article class=\"rec\">\n    <header class=\"rec__head\">\n      <span class=\"rec__rank\">#2</span>\n      <h3 class=\"rec__title\">Duplicate-argument replay detector + cached inline + escalation</h3>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--conf\">conf 0.88</span>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--high\">high</span>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--low\">effort: low</span>\n    </header>\n    <dl class=\"rec__meta\">\n      <dt>Evidence</dt>\n      <dd>537 exact-replay calls (tool + args byte-identical). Concentrated in long sessions — 89/317 in <code>test pi chrome</code>, 77/414 in the implementation-notes loop. Zero new information for non-zero cost.</dd>\n      <dt>Action</dt>\n      <dd>Session-scoped LRU keyed by (tool, normalized_args) for <em>idempotent</em> tools (<code>Read</code>, <code>Grep</code>, <code>find_files</code>, <code>ctx_search</code>, <code>ctx_execute_file</code>). 2nd identical call returns cached result with <code>[cached]</code> marker; 3rd forces a planning turn; 4th escalates to summarize-and-handoff. Bash / network fetches stay non-cacheable.</dd>\n      <dt>Expected outcome</dt>\n      <dd>Directly trims input-token spend on the long-session tail; visibly shortens sessions that loop on the same Read/Grep.</dd>\n    </dl>\n  </article>\n\n  <article class=\"rec\">\n    <header class=\"rec__head\">\n      <span class=\"rec__rank\">#3</span>\n      <h3 class=\"rec__title\">PreToolUse orchestration gate on session-first multi-file mutations</h3>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--conf\">conf 0.82</span>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--high\">high</span>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--med\">effort: medium</span>\n    </header>\n    <dl class=\"rec__meta\">\n      <dt>Evidence</dt>\n      <dd><code>workflow</code> calls = <strong>0/385</strong>. <code>subagent</code> calls in <strong>18%</strong> of sessions (target floor in AGENTS.md: &gt;30%). Cross-corpus subagent / (write+edit+bash) = <strong>0.035</strong> — 10× under the explicit floor. Mechanism documented in AGENTS.md HARD RULE point 4: prose loses to conversational tempo.</dd>\n      <dt>Action</dt>\n      <dd>Extension hook <code>orchestration-gate</code> (same shape as context-mode's PreToolUse routing). When the <em>first</em> Write/Edit/Bash-mutate of a session touches &gt;1 directory or creates &gt;1 new file AND prior subagent dispatches = 0, block. Return structured remediation naming <code>/parallel-research</code>, <code>/parallel-context-build</code>, or scout-async. Explicit <code>--ack-skip-orchestration &lt;reason&gt;</code> bypass, logged for self-grading.</dd>\n      <dt>Expected outcome</dt>\n      <dd>Moves subagent adoption from 18% toward the &gt;30% target; cuts parent-context bloat (and downstream $) on the heaviest-cost session class (multi-file scaffolds done inline).</dd>\n    </dl>\n  </article>\n\n  <article class=\"rec\">\n    <header class=\"rec__head\">\n      <span class=\"rec__rank\">#4</span>\n      <h3 class=\"rec__title\">Real-tool few-shot examples + batched-tool description leadership</h3>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--conf\">conf 0.80</span>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--high\">high</span>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--low\">effort: low</span>\n    </header>\n    <dl class=\"rec__meta\">\n      <dt>Evidence</dt>\n      <dd>Parallel/serial ratio <strong>0.127</strong> despite explicit directive. Current system-prompt example uses a fictional <code>example_complex_tool</code> — models pattern-match to examples, not abstractions.</dd>\n      <dt>Action</dt>\n      <dd>(a) Replace the fake-tool example with 2-3 real-tool examples: parallel <code>Read × 3</code>, <code>Grep + find_files + Read</code> for exploration, multi-command <code>ctx_batch_execute</code>. Annotate each \"independent → one block.\" (b) Edit descriptions of <code>ctx_batch_execute</code>, <code>fff_multi_grep</code>, <code>web_search</code> to lead with the batch use-case and add \"Prefer this over single-call X when you have ≥2 independent items.\" (c) Add to <code>ctx_execute</code> description: \"For ≥2 independent commands, use <code>ctx_batch_execute</code> instead.\"</dd>\n      <dt>Expected outcome</dt>\n      <dd>Lift parallel/serial ratio from 0.127 toward 0.25+; cut wall-clock latency on read-heavy turns.</dd>\n    </dl>\n  </article>\n\n  <article class=\"rec\">\n    <header class=\"rec__head\">\n      <span class=\"rec__rank\">#5</span>\n      <h3 class=\"rec__title\">Verify prompt caching is enabled on the stable system-prompt prefix</h3>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--conf\">conf 0.75</span>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--high\">high</span>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--low\">effort: low</span>\n    </header>\n    <dl class=\"rec__meta\">\n      <dt>Evidence</dt>\n      <dd>This session's system prompt alone (skills + AGENTS.md + tool descriptions) is ~30 KB and is identical turn-over-turn within a session. 385 sessions × multi-turn × 30 KB ≈ a meaningful share of $1,951 if NOT cached.</dd>\n      <dt>Action</dt>\n      <dd>Audit pi's Anthropic client wrapper for <code>cache_control: {type:'ephemeral'}</code> on the stable system-prompt block and the skills/AGENTS.md region. Add a regression test asserting prefix-hash stability across turns. If absent, enable.</dd>\n      <dt>Expected outcome</dt>\n      <dd>If currently off: ~90% cut on cached-prefix input cost — plausibly 20-40% of total $1,951. If on: confirms and closes the question.</dd>\n    </dl>\n  </article>\n\n  <article class=\"rec\">\n    <header class=\"rec__head\">\n      <span class=\"rec__rank\">#6</span>\n      <h3 class=\"rec__title\">Block interactive-TTY commands at the Bash tool boundary</h3>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--conf\">conf 0.78</span>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--high\">high</span>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--low\">effort: low</span>\n    </header>\n    <dl class=\"rec__meta\">\n      <dt>Evidence</dt>\n      <dd>\"sudo: a terminal is required to read the password\" loop pattern across bash's 271 errors (5.6% rate). Loop shape (repeat-until-timeout) is a harness affordance bug — the failure looks like \"no output\" rather than \"needs TTY\", so the model retries.</dd>\n      <dt>Action</dt>\n      <dd>Pre-flight Bash commands against a deny/needs-TTY list (<code>sudo</code> without <code>-n</code>, <code>ssh</code> interactive, <code>vim</code>, <code>less</code> without piping). Return a structured error naming the cause (\"requires TTY; rerun with <code>sudo -n</code> or pipe input\") instead of letting the process hang.</dd>\n      <dt>Expected outcome</dt>\n      <dd>Removes a contributor to both the 681 failed-retries and long-session tail durations.</dd>\n    </dl>\n  </article>\n\n  <article class=\"rec\">\n    <header class=\"rec__head\">\n      <span class=\"rec__rank\">#7</span>\n      <h3 class=\"rec__title\">Fuzzy-fallback Edit.oldText anchoring + stale-cache invalidation</h3>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--conf\">conf 0.82</span>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--high\">high</span>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--med\">effort: medium</span>\n    </header>\n    <dl class=\"rec__meta\">\n      <dt>Evidence</dt>\n      <dd>Edit's 6.3% error rate is dominated by \"oldText not unique / not found\" — usually whitespace / CRLF drift, or anchoring against a stale Read cache after another tool mutated the file. The Read-retry-after-Edit pattern is the signature of anchor staleness, not the model picking bad anchors.</dd>\n      <dt>Action</dt>\n      <dd>Two-tier match: exact first, then whitespace-normalized (CRLF/LF, trailing whitespace, tab/space drift). Accept only if exactly one normalized candidate; otherwise return the candidate list for disambiguation. Hook write tools to bump a per-path version counter that invalidates Read caches.</dd>\n      <dt>Expected outcome</dt>\n      <dd>Cuts Edit-retry-after-Read churn — contributor to both failed-retries (681) and dup-arg Reads (subset of 537).</dd>\n    </dl>\n  </article>\n\n  <article class=\"rec\">\n    <header class=\"rec__head\">\n      <span class=\"rec__rank\">#8</span>\n      <h3 class=\"rec__title\">Per-session cost + orchestration telemetry ledger (JSONL)</h3>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--conf\">conf 0.90</span>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--high\">high</span>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--med\">effort: medium</span>\n    </header>\n    <dl class=\"rec__meta\">\n      <dt>Evidence</dt>\n      <dd>This very analysis ran on aggregate-only data; per-session cost histogram, model/tier distribution, task-class breakdown, per-error-cluster counts, and per-session orchestration ratios are <em>not</em> in the corpus. Every recommendation below 0.85 confidence carries residual uncertainty for this reason.</dd>\n      <dt>Action</dt>\n      <dd>Cost-and-orchestration hook appending JSONL to <code>~/.pi/telemetry/{cost,orchestration}.jsonl</code>: <code>{session_id, task_class, tool, model, input_tokens, output_tokens, cached_tokens, cost_usd, ts}</code> plus per-session rollup <code>{write_n, edit_n, bash_mutate_n, subagent_n, async_n, workflow_n, ratio}</code>. Ship <code>pi cost</code> and <code>pi sessions analyze --orchestration</code> CLIs. Local-only, opt-in for any upload.</dd>\n      <dt>Expected outcome</dt>\n      <dd>Converts ≥10 second-tier items from \"directional 0.55-0.75\" to measured numbers within a week of new data. Indirect impact but the highest-leverage <em>enabler</em>.</dd>\n    </dl>\n  </article>\n\n  <article class=\"rec\">\n    <header class=\"rec__head\">\n      <span class=\"rec__rank\">#9</span>\n      <h3 class=\"rec__title\">Hard tool-call ceiling with forced-summarization at p99 (~260 calls)</h3>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--conf\">conf 0.78</span>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--high\">high</span>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--med\">effort: medium</span>\n    </header>\n    <dl class=\"rec__meta\">\n      <dt>Evidence</dt>\n      <dd>p99 = 258 tool calls; max = <strong>414</strong>. The ~60% gap above p99 is the long tail consistent with runaway loops, not legitimately large jobs. Reinforced by the failed-retry + dup-arg counts concentrating in those same sessions.</dd>\n      <dt>Action</dt>\n      <dd>Circuit-breaker at ~260 calls: inject a synthetic system turn forcing summarize-to-disk → declare remaining work as todos → hand off to a fresh-context continuation that inherits the digest. Non-destructive. Exempt sessions whose recent N calls show diverse tool/arg signatures.</dd>\n      <dt>Expected outcome</dt>\n      <dd>Bounds worst-case session $. Capping the max-414 sessions at ~260 with handoff trims ~150 calls × avg-cost from the worst sessions — disproportionate $ impact on the long-tail.</dd>\n    </dl>\n  </article>\n\n  <article class=\"rec\">\n    <header class=\"rec__head\">\n      <span class=\"rec__rank\">#10</span>\n      <h3 class=\"rec__title\">Flip <code>subagent</code> dispatch default to <code>async: true</code></h3>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--conf\">conf 0.72</span>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--med\">medium</span>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--low\">effort: low</span>\n    </header>\n    <dl class=\"rec__meta\">\n      <dt>Evidence</dt>\n      <dd>Of subagent-using sessions, only 11/18 ≈ 61% used async. ~40% of delegations block the parent despite AGENTS.md saying \"Foreground is the explicit opt-out, not the default.\" <code>workflow</code> already defaults <code>background: true</code> — precedent exists.</dd>\n      <dt>Action</dt>\n      <dd>Flip schema default of <code>async</code> in the subagent tool definition. Update the system-prompt guideline that currently says <code>async (default: false)</code>. One release of dual-default migration behind a config flag.</dd>\n      <dt>Expected outcome</dt>\n      <dd>Moves toward AGENTS.md's prescribed posture; reduces parent-session context bloat on the 40% currently blocking. Compounds with #3.</dd>\n    </dl>\n  </article>\n</section>",
        "notes": "Emitted 10 recommendation cards verbatim from FINDINGS.md top recommendations section. Effort/impact badges derived from the source table. Ranks match the source ordering."
      }
    }
